+## Lifecycle on beforeSession failure
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, `onError` fires with the same `session` and `error` arguments as any other orchestrator failure and the rejection still reaches the caller ([validated by: fires onError with the session and error and still rejects to the caller when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
+- When `beforeSession` throws, `afterSession` fires after `onError` while `beforeUserInput`, `afterUserInput`, `beforeModelResponse`, `afterModelResponse`, and the provider do not run, so an `afterSession` hook can assume `beforeSession` was entered (and may have partially allocated before failing) while no input hooks, prompt hooks, or model calls ran ([validated by: fires afterSession after onError and skips later turn hooks and provider calls when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L49)).
+
 ## Engine startup
 
 - The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).
 
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
